As the ocean's waves crashed onto the shore,
A symphony of sound, a dance of the tide;
The water's rhythmic pulse, a heartbeat to abide.
The sand, a canvas, waiting to be told,
A story of ebb and flow, of waves that unfold.

The ocean's roar, a voice that whispers low,
A language of the deep, only known to few;
The waves, a chorus, singing in harmony,
A melody of movement, wild and free.

As the tide pulls back, the patterns remain,
A poem of the sea, a message to obtain;
A message of the universe, a code to decipher,
A language of the cosmos, a mystery to retrieve.

The poem speaks of life, of birth and decay;
Of the cycles of nature, in an endless sway;
Of the interconnectedness of all things,
A web of life, where every strand sings.

The poem whispers secrets, of the ocean's heart;
A language of the soul, a work of art;
A symphony of meaning, a harmony to share;
A poem of the sea, a message beyond compare.

The interrobang, a question mark and an exclamation point,
A punctuation mark of wonder, a sign of the unknown;
A call to the unknown, a beckoning to explore;
A poem that asks, "What lies beyond the shore?"

The poem's meaning, a mystery to unfold;
A message of the universe, a story to be told;
A poem of the sea, a language of the deep;
A symphony of meaning, a harmony to keep.

The ocean's poem, a work of art sublime;
A language of the soul, a message to the time;
A symphony of wonder, a harmony to share;
A poem that speaks, "The universe is beyond compare!"

Note: I've used every standard punctuation mark at least once, including semicolons (;), colons (:), and the interrobang (?!).
